"""Render the source-reviewed single-level AMI microphone comparison."""
import json
from html import escape as e
from pathlib import Path
ROOT=Path(__file__).resolve().parents[1]
def render(table):
    path=ROOT/'research/s1-array-contrast/review.json'
    if not path.exists():return ''
    d=json.loads(path.read_text());body='<section class="section" id="ami-array-contrast"><h2>Same P01 context, different AMI microphones</h2><p>'+e(d['finding'])+'</p>'
    body+='<p>Replay level 30 of the pressure test: 198.91 seconds of earlier TS3006c audio, beginning at 110.12 seconds, with every listed answer fact present. Compare the mixed close-talking headsets, one distant microphone (Array1-01), and AMI’s released eight-microphone beamformed signal (MDM8). Root-mean-square (RMS) level measures average signal amplitude; both distant inputs are matched to the headset context RMS, with no clipping.</p>'
    body+='<p>All three use the preserved S1 model, prompt, constrained listening, greedy decoding, full history, 480 ms packets and 40-packet answer window. Each condition starts a fresh session. The headset replay matches '+str(d['original_headset_field_agreement']['identical'])+'/'+str(d['original_headset_field_agreement']['total'])+' original response-field records. The last 0.41 seconds of original source audio and inserted request are shared so that the question-containing packets remain byte-identical after resampling. The spoken request is synthetic; the preceding meeting is recorded AMI speech.</p>'
    body+=table('One question, one context length and one replay per microphone condition; native text and independent speech transcripts are reviewed separately.',['Input','Context gain','Question ASR','Source facts in native / spoken answer'],[[e(c['label']),f"{c['gain_db']:+.2f} dB",e(c['question_asr'] or '(empty)'),str(c['native_facts'])+'/2 · '+str(c['spoken_facts'])+'/2'] for c in d['cases']])
    for c in d['cases']:
        body+='<details id="array-'+e(c['id'],quote=True)+'"><summary>'+e(c['label'])+' — input and actual answer</summary><p><strong>Earlier answer evidence (source 110.12–140.00 s):</strong> C says the files were put in the shared folder, D initially sees only their own presentation, and C identifies the components-design PowerPoint.</p><audio controls preload="none" src="'+e(c['evidence_audio'])+'" aria-label="'+e(c['label'])+' earlier source evidence"></audio><p><strong>Request preview (source 291.03 s onward):</strong> the immediate context followed by the synthetic request, using this condition’s microphone.</p><audio controls preload="none" src="'+e(c['input_preview'])+'" aria-label="'+e(c['label'])+' input preview"></audio><p><strong>Native answer:</strong> '+e(c['speech_text'] or '(empty)')+'</p><audio controls preload="none" src="'+e(c['audio'])+'" aria-label="'+e(c['label'])+' actual S1 answer"></audio><p><strong>Independent speech transcript:</strong> '+e(c['spoken_transcript'] or '(empty)')+'</p><p>'+e(c['reason'])+'</p></details>'
    body+='<p><strong>Scope:</strong> the released beamforming is offline and may use later-audio statistics; this does not test a causal beamformer. Matching RMS controls overall amplitude, while microphone response, reverberation and signal processing still differ. One observed reply per condition does not establish a general beamforming benefit or a history limit. The reference requires both the reported shared-folder placement and the identified components-design PowerPoint, without inventing a completed lookup or a folder outage.</p><p>Source meeting: <a href="https://groups.inf.ed.ac.uk/ami/corpus/">AMI Meeting Corpus</a>, CC BY 4.0. The previews adapt the source through microphone selection, gain adjustment and synthetic question insertion.</p>'
    body+='<p>One H100 SXM 80 GB: Thinker, Talker, MTP and Code2Wav share GPU 0; Parakeet ASR runs on GPU 0 after S1 exits. Cases share one private service and run sequentially with fresh sessions; S2 is off. Maximum one GPU active; allocation '+format(d['gpu_hours'],'.4f')+' GPU hours; currently zero for this completed run. Preparation, review and publication use zero GPUs.</p><p><a href="research/s1-array-contrast/review.json">Reviewed outputs and allocation</a> · <a href="research/s1-array-contrast/protocol.json">Matched input settings and sources</a> · <a href="research/s1-array-contrast/manifest.json">Checksums</a> · <a href="https://groups.inf.ed.ac.uk/ami/AMICorpusMirror/amicorpus/beamformed/TS3006c/">AMI beamformed source</a></p></section>'
    return body
